# The repo is edited on Windows but runs on the Linux box (and, later, on the
# NUST HPC nodes). core.autocrlf=true here rewrites checkouts to CRLF, and a
# shell script with CRLF line endings fails on Linux with a "bad interpreter"
# error on the shebang, because the \r is part of the interpreter path. Pin the
# things that get executed to LF regardless of platform.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
